 It visualizes “Intent Bubbles”—zones of the motor cortex lighting up before a physical action is taken.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"RZYOQIXXYQ"}],"key":"IWjmiQQmL3"}],"key":"b1onV83Ers"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synergy: If SciStream detects a lag in the neural-to-digital link, syGlass can highlight the “bottleneck” area in red within the Commander’s field of view, allowing for an immediate tactical swap or mission abort.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"RA06DAzd3B"}],"key":"xJVD5d33nk"}],"key":"lz0LjHD6MR"}],"key":"udjbMmuQNI"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Augmented Intent”","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"mI6v7dJWu7"}],"identifier":"augmented-intent","label":"“Augmented Intent”","html_id":"augmented-intent","implicit":true,"key":"ZPVHb5ek61"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sensory Injection: The Commander can “push” tactical data directly into the user’s sensory perception. For example, injecting a “thermal sense” or “spatial ping” into the user’s parietal lobe, allowing them to “feel” an enemy’s location without looking at a screen.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"FKQS1o6I6l"}],"key":"QsDNvvlgWV"}],"key":"dwUyIlb1er"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus Steering: By manipulating the XR dashboard, the Commander can boost the user’s visual processing or auditory gain during high-stress moments, effectively “tuning” the user’s brain for the mission.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"m1QKPdBsv3"}],"key":"EW5aGpntPW"}],"key":"w9DrKpQrGG"}],"key":"snwiVwU6fy"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the Physician:","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"qwMglRXGR8"}],"identifier":"for-the-physician","label":"For the Physician:","html_id":"for-the-physician","implicit":true,"key":"Sj8qF57Jwz"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Precision Diagnostic Suite”","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"EmO6ST3eq1"}],"identifier":"precision-diagnostic-suite","label":"“Precision Diagnostic Suite”","html_id":"precision-diagnostic-suite","implicit":true,"key":"q8e01EzjMn"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"syGlass Implementation: Enables “Virtual Micro-Slicing.” The Physician can freeze a SciStream live-feed and use syGlass tools to measure the density of neural firing or track electrode degradation in 1:1 scale.","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"V9fySzPEPT"}],"key":"XSAjt78Xkf"}],"key":"Gi94yuXm9a"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synergy: While inside the syGlass VR environment, the Physician can trigger SciX queries via voice command (e.g., “SciX: Show similar activation patterns in recent epilepsy studies”), with the results appearing as floating windows next to the live 3D brain model.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"WQnDxrgZ1s"}],"key":"r0i3CraWdh"}],"key":"kxtx3cBGUc"}],"key":"cAzKwUW71z"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"LWoZqVwuld"}],"identifier":"sensory-re-calibration","label":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","html_id":"sensory-re-calibration","implicit":true,"key":"lEVX64mkpg"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tactile Mapping: If a user has lost sensation in a limb, the Physician can use syGlass in XR to manually stimulate specific “dead” zones. By “tapping” a virtual neuron in the XR environment, they send a signal to the NESD to trigger a phantom touch for the user.","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"EU6e8BRSa0"}],"key":"qZwbTRYhB6"}],"key":"UHRmtgbm4K"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pain Suppression: The Physician can identify “pain circuits” (hyper-active clusters) and use an XR interface to “dim” those regions, sending inhibitory signals to provide immediate relief.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"X3Gwofoykl"}],"key":"J7LYynqAYx"}],"key":"KS7qLL2VJ6"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SciX Integration: During manipulation, SciX provides real-time “Safety Envelopes.” If the Physician tries to stimulate a region too intensely, SciX flags a clinical study or safety protocol as a HUD overlay in the XR headset.","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"Mu1WWlVAnN"}],"key":"GlvnQJEBQg"}],"key":"NGsmMQYsqT"}],"key":"LeFgyWK6Gt"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Technical Implementation via syGlass & SciStream","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"pghv9PruVh"}],"identifier":"technical-implementation-via-syglass-scistream","label":"Technical Implementation via syGlass & SciStream","html_id":"technical-implementation-via-syglass-scistream","implicit":true,"key":"gT7i0i7CHw"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Haptic Mirroring: Use the syGlass Python API to map XR controller coordinates to the 3D coordinates of the neural implant’s electrode array.","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"b2QCKBj6Ps"}],"key":"vK4SobkXbJ"}],"key":"TeqLZ32sga"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latent Feedback (SciStream): To avoid “sensory lag” (which causes nausea or seizures), SciStream must maintain a sub-10ms round-trip latency between the XR “click” and the neural stimulation.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"jqHqGWKBS7"}],"key":"OEmvAkKCLv"}],"key":"ITCkxshXC0"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Visual-Neural Sync: The XR environment (syGlass) ensures that the visual representation of the brain matches the physical stimulation site with micrometer precision, preventing “misfires” in sensitive brain regions.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"xpQimtRSy2"}],"key":"cNHNXcXRg8"}],"key":"fbqoKgQbbI"}],"key":"thxZDxWhPX"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"eeS6UjEGs4"}],"identifier":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","label":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","html_id":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","implicit":true,"key":"eQPG1DQ4rT"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modern Nanosats (3U to 12U CubeSats) act as Tactical Edge Nodes in orbit.","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"CZv7Mo0x6j"}],"key":"oYQF0TWZYk"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Hardware: The Nanosat carries a Q-NET-compatible laser terminal or a high-frequency Ka-band radio.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"qpyPh8SjUO"}],"key":"P7xp5hoNXl"}],"key":"L1jWuez8az"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Link: The MEG-fiber interface (worn by the user) transmits data to a local ground terminal (running your K3s/Go/Envoy stack). This terminal “uplinks” the encrypted neural stream to the Nanosat.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"Xc1GVSWQGz"}],"key":"QYkH0Iv4s1"}],"key":"EjQJaZEWkW"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Q-NET Extension: Some Nanosats now perform Space-to-Ground Quantum Key Distribution (QKD). The satellite beams entangled photons down to the ground terminal, providing the “Quantum Seed” for your TLS 1.3 tunnel even in areas without physical fiber.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"Nfc3sJ0nnk"}],"key":"Y37MwGp5Fd"}],"key":"XPi8uNzgpm"}],"key":"xhkvbjVCZg"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"ojsZnJjTg3"}],"identifier":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","label":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","html_id":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","implicit":true,"key":"W9cb5wUtsV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSDAP is the NASA/DoD program that buys commercial satellite data (from companies like Planet, Spire, or BlackSky) for government use.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"yQzd57Re0Q"}],"key":"scUzdxm5R1"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contextual Awareness: CSDAP provides high-resolution imagery and RF signals from the user’s specific location.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"J9lydME5Ca"}],"key":"icU2BN669P"}],"key":"T8PphfPzPY"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Fusion: Your Go-based microservice in the cloud merges the “Neural Stream” (what the user is thinking/feeling) with “CSDAP Data” (what the satellites see around the user).","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"owk8bMbjcT"}],"key":"QewZ9GObk5"}],"key":"D2Sr2kJPKm"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: If the user’s neural interface detects a high-stress “threat” response, the system automatically pulls the latest CSDAP SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) imagery of the surrounding 5km to identify potential hazards.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"ekBPN7kFu5"}],"key":"ejxGX7L28v"}],"key":"SmtOpCvaYG"}],"key":"eHC1ZNju2f"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"B1hYfWXwsJ"}],"identifier":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","label":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","html_id":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","implicit":true,"key":"OEj3hcxQZE"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To make this work, your K3s Pods must be “Space-Aware”:\nProtocol Optimization: Standard TCP/IP fails over satellite due to high latency. Your Envoy Wrapper is configured to use QUIC (UDP-based) or SCPS (Space Communications Protocol Specifications) to keep the neural stream fluid.","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"KYiyGeheUY"}],"key":"Oojxk8nCgg"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intermittent Connectivity: The Go driver uses a “Store and Forward” buffer. If the Nanosat passes behind a mountain, the MEG-powered interface stores the neural data in a local Sidecar and bursts it to the satellite once the link is restored.","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"nuTdfNjxnM"}],"key":"Zwi2cwqZ9K"}],"key":"k5qagoXY12"}],"key":"sUYyJmfQZj"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"ONgOumA6fi"}],"identifier":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","label":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","html_id":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","implicit":true,"key":"IG2tj4EPPk"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cross-Domain Identity: Entra ID manages the permissions for the satellite uplink. The Nanosat verifies the user’s Workload Identity before allowing the data to enter the “Space Segment” of the DoDIN.","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"fp6Gm6VdiF"}],"key":"ZZSrEU7li8"}],"key":"Bbzbgq3icx"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Access: A commander at a HQ can view the “CSDAP + Neural” fusion dashboard. Think Neuralink with first person visual and subtitles. They authenticate via Entra ID MFA, and the Envoy Proxy decrypts the satellite-delivered stream in real-time.","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"sSSZMrazM9"}],"key":"Rfpg4SVNZg"}],"key":"wNPxAb9Qd5"}],"key":"CPKcBx7lja"}],"key":"mXcaMzKVRp"}],"key":"rfOdkslqHN"},"references":{"cite":{"order":["Chung_2022"],"data":{"Chung_2022":{"label":"Chung_2022","enumerator":"1","doi":"10.1145/3502181.3531475","html":"Chung, J., Zacherek, W., Wisniewski, A., Liu, Z., Bicer, T., Kettimuthu, R., & Foster, I. (2022). SciStream: Architecture and Toolkit for Data Streaming between Federated Science Instruments. <i>Proceedings of the 31st International Symposium on High-Performance Parallel and Distributed Computing</i>, 185–198. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475\">10.1145/3502181.3531475</a>","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475"}}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Index","url":"/index-15","group":"Dashboard"},"next":{"title":"Biological Assets","url":"/bio-assets-1","group":"Dashboard"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}